  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5341",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the relationship with COR-L105 through multiple pathways, all involving the [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate compound. This compound acts as a target of doxorubicin, which in turn targets P2X purinoceptor 1 or GDM-1, both of which ultimately lead to a final target of COR-L105. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin exerts its effects via a mechanism that involves the activation of P2X purinoceptors or the binding of a specific compound to GDM-1, which then modulates COR-L105. The shared involvement of [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate in these pathways indicates a potential common mechanism, possibly involving the modulation of purinoceptor activity or the activation of a signaling cascade downstream of these receptors. The final score of 0.5684 across the three paths suggests a plausible, though not definitive, link between doxorubicin and COR-L105, supported by the consistent involvement of a shared compound in the target pathways.",
